sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If two numbers are relatively prime, then any number which measures one of them is relatively prime to the remaining number.
----
proof:

Let {A} and {B} be two numbers relatively prime, and let any number {C} measure {A}.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="150" height="250" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="VII.23 diagram" src="propVII23.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // A and B are the given numbers relatively prime; C measures A, and D is
    // the supposed common measure of C and B. Line segments only, so the walk
    // is highlight beats. The reductio's D is withdrawn once the
    // contradiction is reached.
    //
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): the lineSlider ends A1, A2,
    // B1, B2, C1, D1 and the off-canvas, colourless rail ends. C1 and D1
